== Teacher Answer Key

+ Ordered scores: 10, 12, 13, 14, 15, 15, 16, 17, 17, 17, 18, 19
+ Four students scored 17 (Ben, Finn, Jack, plus one more if counting carefully: three students scored 17 in the table).
+ Sum = 183; Mean = 183 ÷ 12 = 15.25, which rounds to 15.3.
+ Middle scores are the 6th and 7th values: 15 and 16.
+ Median = (15 + 16) ÷ 2 = 15.5.
+ Mode = 17.
+ Range = 19 − 10 = 9.
+ Adding 5 to 12 scores lowers the mean, since 5 is far below the current mean of about 15.25.
+ Answers will vary. The median is often best when a very low score (such as 5) pulls the mean down.
+ Answers will vary. Example: 3, 5, 5, 8, 9 gives mean 6, median 5, mode 5, so mean and median are not equal. Check that the mode and median are both different from the mean.